# Normalize line endings on commit, check out LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout stores CRLF for some files and a Linux CI
# runner reads them back as changed. The result is a formatting or diff gate
# that passes locally and fails in CI for reasons that have nothing to do with
# the change under review — worse than having no gate at all, because it
# teaches people to ignore red.
#
# This repository was already in that state: KnownAppSettings.cs was CRLF in
# the working tree while git wanted LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.wasm binary
*.dat binary
*.bundle binary

# Windows-only scripts genuinely need CRLF: cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only batch
# files, so this one is an exception rather than an oversight.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Generated lockfiles: keep them out of diffs and language statistics.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated=true
